libstdc++: use the mingw-w64 CRT's __cxa_thread_atexit

The CRT has provided __cxa_thread_atexit in libmingw32.a since
mingw-w64 v8, but the configure link check for it runs only for native
builds, and the mingw32 case in crossconfig.m4 did not check. So cross
builds compiled libstdc++'s own fallback, which registers its cleanup
with atexit() on the first thread_local construction. Statics
constructed later are destroyed before the main thread's thread_local
objects, which violates [basic.start.term]. Check for the CRT function
in cross builds too, as other targets in crossconfig.m4 already do.

On msvcrt this needs mingw-w64 a394c23a51 (src/mingw
tls-atexit-order.patch), without which the CRT version runs those
destructors after every static destructor. MSYS2 fixes this with an
unconditional define instead (msys2/MSYS2-packages#6872). The configure
hunk is what autoconf generates for this check elsewhere.

Known limitation: on Windows XP, a thread_local destructor in a DLL
loaded with LoadLibrary never runs. XP does not run TLS callbacks for
dynamically loaded DLLs, so the CRT's tls_atexit.c never initializes
and __cxa_thread_atexit fails. The libstdc++ fallback instead pinned
the DLL and ran the destructor at process exit. DLLs linked at load
time are unaffected, and on later Windows versions the destructor now
runs at FreeLibrary rather than at exit.

---
 libstdc++-v3/configure      |   11 +++++++++++
 libstdc++-v3/crossconfig.m4 |    1 +
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/libstdc++-v3/crossconfig.m4
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/crossconfig.m4
@@ -196,6 +196,7 @@
     GLIBCXX_CHECK_STDLIB_SUPPORT
     AC_CHECK_FUNCS(aligned_alloc posix_memalign memalign _aligned_malloc)
     AC_CHECK_FUNCS(_wfopen)
+    AC_CHECK_FUNCS(__cxa_thread_atexit)
     GCC_CHECK_TLS
     ;;
   *-netbsd* | *-openbsd*)
--- a/libstdc++-v3/configure
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/configure
@@ -45891,8 +45891,19 @@
 fi
 done
 
+    for ac_func in __cxa_thread_atexit
+do :
+  ac_fn_c_check_func "$LINENO" "__cxa_thread_atexit" "ac_cv_func___cxa_thread_atexit"
+if test "x$ac_cv_func___cxa_thread_atexit" = xyes; then :
+  cat >>confdefs.h <<_ACEOF
+#define HAVE___CXA_THREAD_ATEXIT 1
+_ACEOF
 
+fi
+done
 
+
+
    # Check whether --enable-tls was given.
 if test "${enable_tls+set}" = set; then :
   enableval=$enable_tls;
